{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"curl --insecure -L --max-time 20 --silent --show-error https://www.actuariesindia.org/about-iai | rg -in -C 5 'statutory body|Actuaries Act, 2006|Department of Financial Services|regulating the profession'\"","aggregated_output":"4-    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n5-<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.actuariesindia.org/about-iai\" />\n6-<meta name=\"description\" content=\"About IAI - \n7-The Institute of Actuaries of India\n8-\n9:The Institute of Actuaries of India (IAI) is a statutory body established by an Act of Parliament, viz. The Actuaries Act, 2006 for regulating the profession of Actuaries in India. The nodal ministry for the Institute is Department of Financial Services, Ministry of Finance. | Institute of Actuaries of India\" />\n10-<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"Page not found\" />\n11-<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.json\" />\n12-<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#000000\" />\n13-<meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"Drupal 8 (https://www.drupal.org)\" />\n14-<meta name=\"MobileOptimized\" content=\"width\" />\n--\n1794-  <div class=\"node__content clearfix\">\n1795-    \n1796-            <div property=\"schema:text\" class=\"clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item\"><div class=\"pl-0 m-auto rightsection mt-3\">\n1797-<p class=\"line-bottom font-weight-size\">The Institute of Actuaries of India</p>\n1798-\n1799:<p>The Institute of Actuaries of India (IAI) is a statutory body established by an Act of Parliament, viz. The Actuaries Act, 2006 for regulating the profession of Actuaries in India. The nodal ministry for the Institute is Department of Financial Services, Ministry of Finance.</p>\n1800-\n1801:<p>The affairs of the IAI are managed by a Council in accordance with the provisions of the Actuaries Act, 2006. The Council consists of 12 elected fellow members and 2 persons nominated by Central Government. Currently, two government nominees are from Department of Financial Services and one from Insurance Regulatory Development Authority.</p>\n1802-\n1803-<p>The erstwhile Actuarial Society of India (ASI) was established in September 1944. Since 1979, the ASI has been a Full Member of International Actuarial Association (an umbrella organization to all actuarial bodies across the world) and is actively involved in its affairs. In 1982, the ASI was registered under Registration of Literary, Scientific and Charitable Societies Act XXI of 1860 and Bombay Public Charitable Trust Act, 1950. In 1989, the ASI started examinations upto Associate level, and in 1991, started conducting Fellowship level examination leading to professional qualification of an actuary. Till then, the accreditation was based on Institute of Actuaries, London examinations (now Institute and Faculty of Actuaries).</p>\n1804-\n1805-<p>The Head Office of the Institute is at Seawoods, Navi Mumbai.</p>\n1806-\n--\n2069-                    alt=\"Logo\"></a>\n2070-\n2071-                <h5>About Us</h5>\n2072-\n2073-                <p>\n2074:                    Institute of Actuaries of India (IAI) IAI is a statutory body established under The Actuaries Act 2006\n2075-\t\t\t\t\t (35 of 2006) for regulation of profession of Actuaries in India.\n2076-                </p>\n2077-\n2078-            </div>\n2079-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
